t":true,"url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-09","committee":"North Area Council","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-11","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-19","committee":"Dearne Area Council","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Penistone Area Council","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"North Area Council","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-18","committee":"South Area Council","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Full Council","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Barnsley Council accepts electronic records gap it cannot afford to fix","lead":"Barnsley Council's governance and compliance board has formally agreed to accept a risk in electronic records management, determining that available solutions to fix the problem are too expensive to implement. Staff continue reviewing paper records for disposal, but the electronic records management issue remains unresolved. The board's decision reflects resource constraints the council faces in balancing competing budget demands across its services. Electronic records management has not been prioritised for spending at this time.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"5. Annual Governance Statement Action Plan Update","paper_url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s137782/137782.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"5. Annual Governance Statement Action Plan Update","paper_url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s137782/137782.pdf","headline":"Reducing agency staffing costs is identified as the top workforce priority, indicating current high agency reliance.","detail":"The workforce planning section lists 'reduce agency reliance' as the primary objective under recruitment and attraction, suggesting the council currently has elevated agency spending levels it needs to bring down as part of its broader efficiency strategy.","category":"people","matters":"High agency staffing costs directly reduce operational efficiency and financial flexibility; councils prioritizing reduction typically indicate they view current spending in this area as unsustainably elevated.","figures":"None provided","quote":"Reduce agency reliance, upskill on and streamline recruitment processes, enhance employer branding","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"5. Annual Governance Statement Action Plan Update","paper_url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s137782/137782.pdf","headline":"Council is tolerating an electronic records management compliance risk due to cost constraints.","detail":"The Governance and Compliance Board has formally approved tolerating a risk around electronic records management specifically because the solutions are too expensive to implement. Paper records are being reviewed for disposal but the electronic records compliance gap remains unresolved.","category":"governance","matters":"Accepting known control weaknesses for cost reasons indicates the council is operating with known gaps and prioritizing cost control over compliance remediation, relevant to understanding the control environment and financial governance capacity.","figures":"None provided","quote":"risk tolerated around electronic records given costs of solutions","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"North East Area Council","paper_title":"Item 8 - Commissioning and Financial Update -Sept 2026","paper_url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s137575/137575.pdf","headline":"Drug and Alcohol Outreach service depends on \u00a320,000 annual match funding from Integrated Care Board, confirmed through July 2027.","detail":"The outreach worker service achieved 93% client engagement against a 67% average, with clients achieving an average of 8 positive outcomes each. The Integrated Care Board confirmed in March 2026 it would provide \u00a320,000 match funding for the third year of delivery. Withdrawal of this external funding would require the council to find replacement funding or reduce service.","category":"income","matters":"Service sustainability depends on time-limited external funding commitments; ICB withdrawal would force immediate budget reallocation or service cuts.","figures":"\u00a320,000 ICB match funding; 93% client engagement rate (vs 67% BRS average); delivery confirmed to July 2027","quote":"Following a meeting of Communities DMT and the Place Partnership Delivery Group in March 2026, it was confirmed that \u00a320,000.00 match funding would be provided by the Integrated Care Board to fund the outreach worker in the third year of delivery.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"North East Area Council","paper_title":"Item 8 - Commissioning and Financial Update -Sept 2026","paper_url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s137575/137575.pdf","headline":"Area Council is budgeted to spend \u00a345,750 above its annual allocation, funded from accumulated reserves.","detail":"The Area Council's proposed budget of \u00a3445,750 for 2026/27 exceeds its \u00a3400,000 annual allocation by \u00a345,750. This overspend is described as 'feasible due to carry forward from previous years'. The carry-forward balance reduces from \u00a3147,225.59 to \u00a3121,475.59 as a result of this planned spending.","category":"reserves","matters":"Shows the council is using accumulated reserves to fund current-year spending above base allocation, reducing financial flexibility if service demands increase further.","figures":"\u00a345,750 overspend; \u00a3400,000 base allocation; \u00a3445,750 total planned spend; carry-forward reducing from \u00a3147,225.59 to \u00a3121,475.59","quote":"The proposed budget would take the Area Council approximately \u00a345,750.00 over budget for the financial year 2026/27. This is feasible due to carry forward from previous years.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"6b. Appendix A - PLANS VS OUTTURN 25-26","paper_url":"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s136552/136552.pdf","headline":"Goldthorpe Towns Fund programme only 2% deployed: \u00a34.3m allocation had just \u00a397k outturn","detail":"Goldthorpe Towns Fund - DLUHC shows planned expenditure of \u00a34,302,481 but actual outturn of only \u00a397,276, representing an underspend of \u00a34,205,205 (98%).","category":"capital","matters":"Towns Fund is external government regeneration financing with specific deployment requirements and clawback provisions; a 98% underspend indicates delivery failure on externally-funded strategic programme and may affect future funding tranches","figures":"Planned: \u00a34,302,481; Actual: \u00a397,276; Underspend: \u00a34,205,205 (98%)","quote":"Goldthorpe Towns Fund - DLUHC 4,302,481 97,276 -4,205,205","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-16"},"name":"Barnsley","findings_total":63,"news_drafts_total":1}}